    <briefdescription>
<para>Type-erased owning handle to a dense coefficient vector held by a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_concrete_vector_arithmetic" kindref="compound">ConcreteVectorArithmetic</ref>&lt;<ref refid="class_ring" kindref="compound">Ring</ref>&gt;</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Stores a single <computeroutput>void*</computeroutput> whose concrete type is the wrapped ring&apos;s <computeroutput>ElementContainerType</computeroutput> (e.g. an <computeroutput>std::vector&lt;elem&gt;</computeroutput> or an <ref refid="class_a_ring" kindref="compound">ARing</ref> concrete array). All payload access is funneled through <computeroutput><ref refid="class_concrete_vector_arithmetic" kindref="compound">ConcreteVectorArithmetic</ref></computeroutput> <mdash/> the friend declaration <mdash/> so only the matching arithmetic dispatcher can recover the real pointer. Default-constructed as null; copies are disallowed and moves go through <computeroutput><ref refid="class_element_array_a394e678fb334b143b42102ec2c9c33a7_1a394e678fb334b143b42102ec2c9c33a7" kindref="member">swap</ref></computeroutput>, keeping ownership unique. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
